Hi there, Cyranos! Thanks for asking. The current President of the
Board of Directors of the Logical Language Group is also the Chair of
Penguicon (that's me). I'm providing facilities to host a Lojban
Festival as part of Penguicon this year, which is why we're talking
about it here.

Penguicon is a convention of about a thousand people in southeast
Michigan, right down the street from Metro Detroit Airport in Romulus.
It is three weeks from now on the weekend of May 1 through 3. It
brings together science fiction, open source software, and other geek
interests. Preregistration costs $45 ($50 at the door), and although
our conference hotel is full, the hotels next door are not.

More information is available at http://penguicon.org, but feel free
to email me with specific questions.

-Eppcott


